  (text "CC / CV CONTROL - DIRECT DUAL 100k DIGIPOT"
    (at 25.4 20.32 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.778 1.778) (bold yes)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid "1448aafa-9493-420f-892d-7095bb14092b")
  )
  (text "J7 / J9: 1=A, 2=W, 3=B. Six independent terminals; no A/W straps or forced ground.\nNo automatic manual fallback and no relay coil consumption."
    (at 25.4 35.56 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid "bcc5d4b9-92d4-4194-a833-d35901b4f6d1")
  )
  (text "POWER LOGIC AND INITIALIZE BOTH CODES BEFORE ENABLING THE CONVERTER.\nNo defined safe CC/CV setpoint with 3V3 absent. Stop the converter before logic power loss.\nWith valid VDD, idle SPI retains the last code; POR / reset sets both wipers to 0x80.\nMidscale is not inherently a safe voltage or current for an unknown converter."
    (at 25.4 120.65 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27) (bold yes)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid "920f7a58-8e6d-490f-9260-1359db802b85")
  )
  (text "QUALIFY THE EXTERNAL INTERFACE BEFORE CONNECTION:\nA / W / B must stay between GND and VDD, with terminal current below +/-1mA.\nAn energized converter must not back-power an unpowered MCP42100 through its terminals.\nCommon ground is required; no galvanic isolation or universal converter compatibility.\nConverter hardware must independently limit voltage / current for the connected receiver."
    (at 25.4 144.78 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid "8150ee82-14a4-4883-830a-c7111fb11bc2")
  )
